Airlock — third-party components and licenses
=============================================

Airlock is an installer/composer. It does NOT bundle the upstream tools below;
each is fetched at install time from its own source. Airlock ships only its own
glue (identity gate, config layer, custom UIs) plus, where noted, patches.

Component         Upstream                          License       How obtained
----------------  --------------------------------  ------------  ----------------------------
ttyd (devterm)    github.com/tsl0922/ttyd           MIT           binary downloaded at install (sha-pinned)
xterm.js (devterm) github.com/xtermjs/xterm.js      MIT           vendored in apps/devterm/web/vendor/ (xterm 5.x + fit/unicode11/web-links addons)
code-server       github.com/coder/code-server      MIT           tarball downloaded at install (sha-pinned)
markserv          npm: markserv                     MIT           npm at install
filebrowser       github.com/filebrowser/filebrowser Apache-2.0   binary downloaded at install (sha-pinned)
markwand assets   github.com/givepro91/markwand     MIT           vendored in apps/markwand/static/ (tokens/enhance/editor/edit-button)
highlight.js      github.com/highlightjs/highlight.js BSD-3-Clause vendored in apps/markwand/static/vendor/highlight.min.js (v11.11.1)
marked            github.com/markedjs/marked        MIT           vendored in apps/markwand/static/vendor/marked.min.js (v15.0.12)
DOMPurify         github.com/cure53/DOMPurify       Apache-2.0 OR MPL-2.0  vendored in apps/markwand/static/vendor/purify.min.js (v3.4.8)
orca (ADE)        github.com/stablyai/orca          MIT           AppImage downloaded at install (sha-pinned)
orca web client   github.com/stablyai/orca          MIT           vendored BUILT dist in apps/orca/web-bundle/dist/ (patched; redistributed)
paseo (CLI)       github.com/getpaseo/paseo         AGPL-3.0      npm i @getpaseo/cli at install (not redistributed)
paseo patches     apps/paseo/patches/               AGPL-3.0      our patches — derivative of paseo, see that dir
paseo web-ui patcher apps/paseo/browse-host/bin/patch-web-ui.js  AGPL-3.0  encodes derivative edits of paseo's web-ui
paseo browse-host apps/paseo/browse-host/ (ours)    MIT           loopback-WS sidecar; needs Playwright (follow-up, not wired in v1)
Playwright/Chromium (only if browse-host used)      Apache-2.0 / (Chromium BSD)  downloaded at install

Everything else under apps/ (hub, publish, notepad, dev-monitor backends/UIs, the
gate, config layer, installers) is Airlock's own code under MIT (repo root LICENSE).

Orca web client (apps/orca/web-bundle/dist/) — derived from stablyai/orca, MIT,
Copyright (c) 2026 Lovecast Inc.; local patches under this repo's MIT license. Unlike
the other upstream tools, this is a BUILT derivative we REDISTRIBUTE (it ships in the
repo and is served at /orca-web/), which the upstream MIT license permits with this
attribution. Provenance + patch summary: apps/orca/web-bundle/README.md.

Deferred to a follow-up (NOT shipped in v1, so not a distribution concern yet):
the paseo browse-host live panels, and the orca local-render / grab sidecars (the
client code for those is in the vendored web-bundle but stays inert without the
services, which this repo does not install).

Notes
-----
- Downloaded binaries (orca AppImage, ttyd, code-server, filebrowser, Chromium)
  are NOT redistributed by Airlock; the installer fetches them from upstream and
  verifies sha256 where applicable. Operators accept the upstream terms of those
  binaries.
- Mixed-license: the Airlock core is MIT. Paseo (@getpaseo/cli) is AGPL-3.0 and
  runs as a SEPARATE PROCESS — the core talks to it over loopback IPC/WS, so the
  core is not a derivative of paseo (mere aggregation). The paseo *patches* and the
  *web-ui patcher* ARE derivatives of paseo and carry AGPL-3.0; the browse-host
  sidecar is an independent program (no paseo imports) and is MIT. The full
  AGPL-3.0 text is vendored at apps/paseo/patches/LICENSE. This is NOT legal advice.
- Vendored (redistributed) libraries: unlike the downloaded binaries above, the
  markwand viewer's client-side libraries — highlight.js (BSD-3-Clause), marked
  (MIT), and DOMPurify (Apache-2.0 OR MPL-2.0) — ARE redistributed in this repo
  under apps/markwand/static/vendor/. Each minified file retains its own upstream
  license header. They are self-hosted so the viewer loads no external CDN.
- Brand icons: apps/orca/orca.png and apps/paseo/paseo.png (both moved
  in-app with their app-package-contract migrations — child 4 P2b — and
  staged by the platform from there now) are the upstream projects' own
  logos, vendored for the launcher tiles (nominative use — identifying the
  tool each tile opens), and are their respective trademarks, not
  MIT-licensed Airlock code. The Airlock porthole mark
  (hub/assets/apple-touch-icon.png, favicon.png;
  artwork bin/airlock-mark.png; generator bin/gen-hub-icons.py) is the author's
  own under the repo-root MIT license. So is the per-app icon set — the glyph
  sprite in hub/index.html, the favicons and iOS home-screen icons it produces
  (hub/assets/app-icons/*.svg and *.png, apps/devterm/web/favicon.svg and
  apple-touch-icon.png, and the inline mark in apps/code-server/web/shell.html),
  and their generator bin/gen-app-icons.py. Those glyphs are drawn for this
  repo — generic marks for the kind of tool each tile opens, not any upstream
  project's logo.
